# Ctrl+Z

Before large or destructive file changes, run a snapshot:

```bash
npx ctrl-z snap -m "<short description of upcoming change>"
```

If this repo is the Ctrl+Z source itself:

```bash
node src/cli.js snap -m "<short description>"
```

When the user wants to undo agent damage:

1. `node src/cli.js list` (or `npx ctrl-z list`)
2. `node src/cli.js restore 1 --yes`

Do not delete `.ctrl-z/`. Do not claim files are unrecoverable without checking the snapshot list first.

Note: Cursor does not auto-hook snapshots; you must snap explicitly. Claude Code with the plugin gets automatic snapshots.
